***REMOVED*** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
***REMOVED*** ntfy Secret — /etc/ntfy/server.yml (contains S3 credentials -> SOPS).
***REMOVED*** Mounted subPath: config changes need a pod delete (no hot reload).
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED***   cp ntfy-secret.yaml.example ntfy-secret.yaml
***REMOVED***   $EDITOR ntfy-secret.yaml   ***REMOVED*** fill S3 key/secret
***REMOVED***   sops -e -i ntfy-secret.yaml
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED*** Post-deploy: create admin user against the auth DB on the PVC:
***REMOVED***   kubectl -n ntfy exec deploy/ntfy -- ntfy user add --role=admin bombom
***REMOVED*** (then optionally `ntfy token add bombom` for script/phone access)
***REMOVED*** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: ntfy
  namespace: ntfy
stringData:
  server.yml: |
    base-url: "https://ntfy.example.com"
    cache-file: "/var/cache/ntfy/cache.db"
    cache-duration: "12h"
    auth-file: "/var/cache/ntfy/user.db"
    auth-default-access: "deny-all"
    ***REMOVED*** S3 attachments on storage SeaweedFS. ntfy OWNS this bucket — never reuse it.
    ***REMOVED*** If uploads fail with HTTP/2 stream errors, append &disable_http2=true.
    attachment-cache-dir: "s3://ACCESS_KEY:SECRET@ntfy?region=us-east-1&endpoint=https://storage-s3.lan.example.com:8333"
